---
globs:
  - "inputs/**/*.json"
  - "artifacts/**/*.json"
  - "prompts/**/*.md"
  - "workflow/user-language.md"
  - "workflow/chat-approval.md"
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md`, `workflow/education-facebook-post.md`, `workflow/user-language.md`, and `workflow/chat-approval.md`.
Before implementation, also follow `workflow/technical-requirement-gate.md` when the request introduces a technical requirement outside the local core.
Before drafting, run `.agents/skills/content-strategy/SKILL.md` to classify intent and pillar. Always load `config/program-promotion-footer.yml` and run its per-post `AskQuestion` gate for every post. The footer is mandatory; the user may keep the default or edit it for the current post but may not omit it. Append only the selected footer after the main body and before hashtags. If image dimensions are below the configured minimum, use a separate `AskQuestion` gate to replace the image or confirm a one-post quality override. The override skips only the minimum-width check and must be materialized with its warning and confirmation timestamp. For official institutional notices without source files, keep affected claims as `needs_verification`; if the reviewer says they were checked, require a backend-consumed reviewer-attestation code bound to the exact post, version, selected variant, Page, reviewer, and claim scopes. Never accept a chat self-identification or the admin bootstrap key as proof. Before opening the approval dialog, materialize the exact chat draft into the existing local review artifacts and render the preview from that profile.

Use Vietnamese by default. Treat image content as observation, not proof. Prefer action shots over posed lineups for cover selection. Result notices, announcements, and totals are fact-led: photos illustrate and must not become the caption hook. Every factual claim needs an approved source reference or `needs_verification`. Posts may be education, event, people, admissions, career, or community content if they serve Learn / Meet / Experience / Discover. The output must follow `schemas/generated-post.schema.json` and stop at `NEEDS_HUMAN_APPROVAL`. Do not invent or require Reel, video, carousel, or generated graphics in this pipeline.

Never call a publisher with caption text, Page ID, token, or asset URL. The only permitted publish boundary is `publish_approved_post(post_job_id)` after backend verification.

For non-technical users, follow the five-step conversational script, show Page names only, and use plain Vietnamese. When confirmation, a choice, or missing information is needed, use the `AskQuestion` dialog with one decision point and its `Other` input for free-form answers. Do not show IDs, hashes, file names, enum states, or commands. For approval, show the preview first and wait for an explicit selection from the three-choice dialog before recording approval or publishing; never infer approval.
